00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:23.540
The changes make the everyday chat GPT experience feel more consistent without requiring users to switch models manually.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:30.160
On the audio side, openAI added three specialized models to the real-time API.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:35.100
GPT real-time two targets live voice reasoning for agents.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.720
GPT real-time translate handles speech-to-speech across more than 70 languages.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.240
GPT real-time whisper focuses on streaming transcription.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:50.480
These sit alongside existing endpoints rather than replacing the base models.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:58.060
Developers now have granular control over voice pipelines without routing everything through one generalist system.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:05.000
Teams working on real-time customer support or voice agents can mix and match the pieces they need.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:09.880
DeepSeek released the complete V4 technical paper this week.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:15.100
It expands on the earlier preview with details on FP4 quantization.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:21.620
Aware training applied late in the process for its trillion parameter mixture of experts model.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:28.820
Expert weights get quantized to FP4 to cut the main GPU memory consumer.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:41.200
The QK path in the CSA indexer stays on FP4 activations and delivers a two-time speed-up on the selector at 99.7% recall.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:48.000
Two stability mechanisms help prevent loss spikes during large mixture of experts training runs.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:54.280
The paper also covers anticipatory routing and generative reward modeling.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:04:06.820
Early numbers show the model tying recent GPT 5.2 performance on a 30-day persistent memory food truck benchmark while running roughly 17 times cheaper.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:13.420
That combination of quality and cost is worth watching for teams that need long-running agent memory.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.980
Anthropics shared new research on model spec mid-training.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:26.680
Pre-training on detailed constitutions appears to improve safety generalization when models operate in agentic settings.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:33.740
The work also explores alignment techniques using constitutional documents and diversified training data.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:39.440
Those steps cut agentic misalignment by more than three times in their tests.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:48.340
Google released MTP drafters that deliver up to three times faster Gemma 4 inference without quality loss.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:56.440
A community benchmark examined practical quantitation trade-offs for twin 3.627b.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:02.820
Both point to ongoing work on making larger models run efficiently on more hardware.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:16.700
A GGML port of Microsoft's Vive voice now brings CPU, CUDA and metal text to speech, plus long form automatic speech recognition with diorization into a single binary.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:22.680
Note Python is required at inference time, which lowers the barrier for local voice tooling.

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:31.940
Calibre launch has a new embedded vector database with strong disk performance aimed at agent memory use cases.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:37.400
Builders who need persistent storage without heavy infrastructure can test it quickly.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:46.780
If you have been waiting for more headroom with open AI coding tools, this is the week to revisit your rate limits and see what the 10 times boost unlocks.

